{{- /* Shell config is per-platform, and the two must never both land: .bashrc is the
       Arch/Omarchy one (its defaults are bash and ~/.bashrc sources them), .zshrc is
       everywhere else. WezTerm and Amethyst go the same way -- Omarchy supplies its own
       terminal, themed by its own switcher, and Hyprland is the tiling WM. */}}
{{- if (eq (includeTemplate "is-arch" .) "true") }}
.zshrc
.config/wezterm/wezterm.lua
{{- /* tmux: adopt Omarchy's config rather than ours. Its 4185-byte config already sets
       everything ours did -- mouse, history-limit 50000, escape-time, base-index 1,
       renumber-windows, truecolor (via terminal-overrides *:RGB), set-clipboard,
       focus-events, vi copy mode, splits in the pane's cwd -- and adds a whole
       keybinding scheme whose `-N` descriptions are what omarchy-menu-tmux-keybindings
       prints. Its prefix is C-Space with C-b kept as prefix2, so muscle memory survives.

       The reason not to deploy ours is not the theme switcher: omarchy-theme-set-tmux
       only pushes vars into running sessions with `tmux set-environment` and never
       touches the file. It is omarchy-update's migrations, which edit
       ~/.config/tmux/tmux.conf in place with sed -i and >> (three of the 120 do). Ours
       and Omarchy's are the same path since #81, so chezmoi and those migrations would
       take turns overwriting each other.

       What Arch gives up: `terminal-features ",xterm*:hyperlinks"` (OSC 8) and the
       | and - split binds. Omarchy has neither. */}}
.config/tmux/tmux.conf
{{- /* Fonts: Omarchy's terminal is configured for JetBrainsMono Nerd Font and Hack has
       zero faces installed there. Our only Hack consumer is WezTerm, which is ignored
       above. Deploying seven font files nothing references. */}}
.local/share/fonts
{{- /* starship.toml is deliberately NOT ignored. Nothing in Omarchy rewrites it after
       install -- no migration mentions it and no bin/ script writes it -- so chezmoi can
       own it safely, and ours now carries Omarchy's prompt design plus the kubernetes
       module. See dot_config/starship.toml. */}}
{{- /* zsh plugin clones from .chezmoiexternal: nothing sources them here, since .zshrc
       is not deployed and the login shell is bash. */}}
.zsh
{{- else }}
.bashrc
{{- end }}
